We have derived improved differentiability properties for solutions to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
  \begin{equation*}
  \min \left\{\iint_{\Omega}e^{2\alpha|D^2u|}dxdt:\ u\in \mathcal{K}_\psi(\Omega),\ u=x\text{ in }\Omega\cap\{t\geq \tau\}\right\}.
  \end{equation*}
  Given that the obstacle function is smooth and non-constant, and under the condition $\frac{1}{p-1}-\beta\in H^1_0(0,\tau), $ we have shown that the solution to this problem is characterised by weak symmetrisability of its Hessian, and this leads to the weak continuity of the determinant of the Hessian of the solution for $s=\frac{3}{p}-1\in (1,2).$
